--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
found no match for symbol
dropped the body
--
N5008 [conv.qual] concerns the cv-qualifiers const and volatile; GNU
`__restrict' is not weighed in a qualification conversion by GCC or Clang.
glibc declares `strtod(const char *__restrict, char **__restrict)' and
`mbsrtowcs(wchar_t *, const char **__restrict, ...)'; a `char **' argument
found no viable candidate, so libc++'s __do_strtod<float/double/long double>
and the __libcpp_*_l locale wrappers were dropped (280 drops over the libc++
tests of the corpus).
